repo_all_commit_info_list.description:
version 2.0

- A new User_Inputs.py file with better structure and description of parameters, including dictionaries;
- Function to check user inputs at pré start;
- Less processing folders (6), now numbered and containing all necessary information;
- Julia Random Forest classification disabled from main script until it has easy to setup instructions and until it works on macOS;
- Supports 3 machine learning algorithms (Random Forest, XGBoost and Unet);
- Configs and Functions are now called configs and modules. Classification_Workflow.py is now called workflow.py;
- Restructured code, although still not the best optimisation, many redundant variables and functions were deleted;
- Now the majority of the processing is based on stacks and not single TIF files;
- Ability to split large images into patches, classify each one and then mosaic all (valid for all ML algorithms);
- Now checks if .env file with credentials is available.

